<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Smertrios</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Smertrius</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Smertrios was a Celtic god known from Roman-period inscriptions in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhineland">Rhineland</a>, including the Pillar of the Boatmen in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, where he is shown as a bearded figure raising a club against a serpent. Often compared with Hercules or Mars, he is thought by many scholars to have been a god of providence or protection. Some link his name with the Smertae of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/smertrios.jpg" alt="Smertrios" width="320" height="199" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. Clio20 assumed (based on copyright claims). · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Le_Pilier_des_Nautes_06.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
